                    {
                        "sense_id": "8aeb2073-3392-3f13-95f4-0e09c59267a3",
                        "entry_id": "22cbfaa0-f89c-3efa-a9b2-463737960796",
                        "glosses": [
                            "artysta cyrkowy żonglujący różnymi przedmiotami"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d1f1f992-a97a-4c98-917b-bea2dfb04c86",
                                "sense_id": "8aeb2073-3392-3f13-95f4-0e09c59267a3",
                                "text": "Oprócz połykaczy ognia na pokazie wystąpili też żonglerzy."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8fa70d49-dae0-348d-a6eb-c2615dec8e7c",
                        "entry_id": "22cbfaa0-f89c-3efa-a9b2-463737960796",
                        "glosses": [
                            "muzykant, śpiewak i tancerz w średniowieczu"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.2\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ab1cd1b8-5633-4db2-87ff-8415ce56a54e",
                        "source_entry_id": "22cbfaa0-f89c-3efa-a9b2-463737960796",
                        "source_sense_id": "8aeb2073-3392-3f13-95f4-0e09c59267a3",
                        "target_lang_word": "juggler",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "juggler",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7f5a8c24-e4f5-3fac-addb-727da9a7d135",
                                        "entry_id": "f1bd87f4-8555-3f17-b664-0c08f41db983",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Agent noun of juggle; one who either literally juggles objects, or figuratively juggles tasks."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "agent",
                                            "form-of"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c354c3c1-307d-4dfe-b3f7-2251b49b2170",
                                                "sense_id": "7f5a8c24-e4f5-3fac-addb-727da9a7d135",
                                                "text": "Baraka was part trickster and part provocateur, a brilliant juggler of genres, ideas, and identities, whose career spanned nearly six decades."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "65055818-797b-4b74-b228-a83a6843d489",
                                                "sense_id": "7f5a8c24-e4f5-3fac-addb-727da9a7d135",
                                                "text": "2016, Jule Scherer, “Going out for the first time as a mum,” stuff.co.nz, 15 March, 2016,\nSince the babies were born I’ve turned into a 24/7 milking machine, a bilingual nursery-rhyme jukebox, a prolific laundress, a bum-wiping wizard, a baby juggler and two-armed synchronised cuddler."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3f1a9468-7d8b-380e-ba0c-b170d28efefb",
                                        "entry_id": "f1bd87f4-8555-3f17-b664-0c08f41db983",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who practices juggling."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f09ce541-896a-42dc-9bc1-0bde9f8efeaa",
                                                "sense_id": "3f1a9468-7d8b-380e-ba0c-b170d28efefb",
                                                "text": "Coming forward and seating himself on the ground in his white dress and tightened turban, the chief of the Indian Jugglers begins with tossing up two brass balls, which is what any of us could do, and concludes with keeping up four at the same time, which is what none of us could do to save our lives, nor if we were to take our whole lives to do it in."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fc4af7d1-88c8-4a37-9896-cbea573937be",
                                                "sense_id": "3f1a9468-7d8b-380e-ba0c-b170d28efefb",
                                                "text": "Thus the whale-line folds the whole boat in its complicated coils, twisting and writhing around it in almost every direction. All the oarsmen are involved in its perilous contortions; so that to the timid eye of the landsman, they seem as Indian jugglers, with the deadliest snakes sportively festooning their limbs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9ab1a025-5db5-401a-88a5-7f36dcca9552",
                                                "sense_id": "3f1a9468-7d8b-380e-ba0c-b170d28efefb",
                                                "text": "The waiters, commanded by Jules, moved softly across the thick Oriental rugs, balancing their trays with the dexterity of jugglers, and receiving and executing orders with that air of profound importance of which only really first-class waiters have the secret."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "656d0b4b-c62b-48f8-8966-11957adcf5b7",
                                                "sense_id": "3f1a9468-7d8b-380e-ba0c-b170d28efefb",
                                                "text": "Only when a juggler misses catching his ball does he appeal to me."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "15c0f797-cce2-3e30-a60b-e10dd936e133",
                                        "entry_id": "f1bd87f4-8555-3f17-b664-0c08f41db983",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who performs tricks using sleight of hand, a conjurer, prestidigitator."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "568326e5-1289-4d12-9eb0-9f4d6ea09372",
                                                "sense_id": "15c0f797-cce2-3e30-a60b-e10dd936e133",
                                                "text": "They ſay this tovvne is full of coſenage: / As nimble Iuglers that deceiue the eie: / Darke vvorking Sorcerers that change the minde: / Soule-killing VVitches, that deforme the bodie: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "44631f84-7227-475a-9284-9267880737b7",
                                                "sense_id": "15c0f797-cce2-3e30-a60b-e10dd936e133",
                                                "text": "[…] Along with them / They brought one Pinch, a hungry lean-faced villain, / A mere anatomy, a mountebank, / A threadbare juggler and a fortune-teller, / A needy, hollow-eyed, sharp-looking wretch, / A dead-looking man: this pernicious slave, / Forsooth, took on him as a conjurer […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a637a763-2f1c-42b1-94f0-93a23932db04",
                                                "sense_id": "15c0f797-cce2-3e30-a60b-e10dd936e133",
                                                "text": "And such captious ſubtleties do indeed often puzzle and ſometimes ſilence men, but rarely ſatisfy them. Being like the tricks of Jugglers, vvhereby men doubt not but they are cheated, though oftentimes they cannot declare by vvhat ſlights they are impoſed on."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "38dcf5d4-d1ea-4695-9549-5cdb5ef49732",
                                                "sense_id": "15c0f797-cce2-3e30-a60b-e10dd936e133",
                                                "text": "Come hither Filch. I am as fond of this Child, as though my Mind miſgave me he vvere my ovvn. He hath as fine a Hand at picking a Pocket as a VVWoman, and is as nimble-finger’d as a Juggler."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ca17e73f-8182-439c-bd07-9ddecae9700e",
                                                "sense_id": "15c0f797-cce2-3e30-a60b-e10dd936e133",
                                                "text": "Doubtless the pleasure is as great / In being cheated, as to cheat. / As lookers-on find most delight, / Who least perceive the juggler’s sleight; / And still the less they understand, / The more admire the sleight of hand."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6d615677-41e1-447a-be79-259103a5e4a0",
                                                "sense_id": "15c0f797-cce2-3e30-a60b-e10dd936e133",
                                                "text": "According to Mr. Gmelin’s account, [the Samojede magicians] are tolerable jugglers. Some have the art of plunging a knife into the body, without making a wound; and apparently wringing off their heads, by fastening a cord round their necks, and suffering two persons to draw it tight, and afterwards setting it on again. But these tricks are seen only among those magicians who require but little art to deceive their countrymen; and, indeed, to speak seriously, such a Siberian juggler, would cut but a very indifferent figure at a European fair."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b9bd0be3-e92d-3dca-b935-b1524b90b133",
                                        "entry_id": "f1bd87f4-8555-3f17-b664-0c08f41db983",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A magician or wizard."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1a1965b4-51d2-48f7-92bd-c7e85909474e",
                                                "sense_id": "b9bd0be3-e92d-3dca-b935-b1524b90b133",
                                                "text": "So far we may follow the 'clerk,' but he subsequently shows himself to be a juggler, and not a worker by regular natural science."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8e31b063-9b59-46ea-bf5f-00449232bcc1",
                                                "sense_id": "b9bd0be3-e92d-3dca-b935-b1524b90b133",
                                                "text": "The contents of the Sūtra is a legend of a juggler Bhadra. Bhadra, due to his magical tricks, intended to deceive the Buddha and invited him to a magic feast which was charmed into being on a refuse dump."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c4e7b501-ff0f-4f4a-9c46-f545dee0aa33",
                                                "sense_id": "b9bd0be3-e92d-3dca-b935-b1524b90b133",
                                                "text": "This time he accidentally takes a juggler's magic ball and embarks on a successful career as a street entertainer. Every time he throws the red ball into the air, the ball multiplies, and magical scenes appear on them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "16212760-6114-468e-9a02-c74399dbe331",
                                                "sense_id": "b9bd0be3-e92d-3dca-b935-b1524b90b133",
                                                "text": "Brauner transforms the Juggler's magic wand into a lunar-solar scepter to symbolize the reunion of opposites, to set up a confrontation of masculine and feminine principles, and to announce their alchemical fusion."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "juggler",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "40002a87-4634-3197-bef8-f344c3b56bff",
                                        "entry_id": "70c076d8-2d17-33f7-bea2-ef8dcaf39942",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Misspelling of jugular."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "misspelling"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ea4632c2-ef13-4a37-94f3-29abab7c26cb",
                                                "sense_id": "40002a87-4634-3197-bef8-f344c3b56bff",
                                                "text": "The defensive system they were playing hampered them from going for the juggler."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b09b5e80-c53b-45a2-ae45-2c7c7ba03aff",
                                                "sense_id": "40002a87-4634-3197-bef8-f344c3b56bff",
                                                "text": "[They] declare that Kashmir is their juggler vein."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d56c5dba-5199-4c63-b6fe-abaf610fbe66",
                        "source_entry_id": "22cbfaa0-f89c-3efa-a9b2-463737960796",
                        "source_sense_id": "8aeb2073-3392-3f13-95f4-0e09c59267a3",
                        "target_lang_word": "žonglér",
                        "target_lang_code": "cs",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "84eb5c00-4f42-48ec-a5ce-ef1d9a6ba7eb",
                        "source_entry_id": "22cbfaa0-f89c-3efa-a9b2-463737960796",
                        "source_sense_id": "8aeb2073-3392-3f13-95f4-0e09c59267a3",
                        "target_lang_word": "jongleur",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "jongleur",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fafc0eff-241f-3eec-acf7-11e4c7724003",
                                        "entry_id": "b381f264-27e3-3ab6-9079-795a2791f99a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Sorte de ménestrel qui allait, chantant des poèmes ou récitant des contes, dans les cours des princes et dans les maisons des grands seigneurs."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "19656b0c-bb19-474a-81b2-b2afe9ae5ece",
                                                "sense_id": "fafc0eff-241f-3eec-acf7-11e4c7724003",
                                                "text": "Il ne manquait dans cette foule bigarrée ni de bouffons ni de jongleurs […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b1c4a674-3ff9-4fbb-8423-1eccd53b0b87",
                                                "sense_id": "fafc0eff-241f-3eec-acf7-11e4c7724003",
                                                "text": "Enfin, le personnage même des troubadours procède des jongleurs, et ceux-ci sont, comme leur nom l’indique, une dérivation de l’ancien joculator, qui faisait partie, aussi bien que les histrions et les mimes, d’une classe d’hommes consacrée aux jeux dégénérés de la scène romaine."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ca639ef2-1c70-4ffd-9a9b-e6307ca0f0da",
                                                "sense_id": "fafc0eff-241f-3eec-acf7-11e4c7724003",
                                                "text": "Nous irons, mes frères et moi, dans les villes, nous nous tiendrons avec un luth sur la place publique, le jour du marché. Les bonnes gens s’approcheront de nous, et nous leur dirons : « Nous sommes les jongleurs du bon Dieu, et nous allons vous chanter un lai. Si vous en êtes contents, vous nous donnerez une récompense. »"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ed8b158-0cee-4023-96d1-6cb4e4c47738",
                                                "sense_id": "fafc0eff-241f-3eec-acf7-11e4c7724003",
                                                "text": "Entre les deux camps se trouve le souk avec tous les éléments d’un marché indigène : marchands, conteurs d’histoires, jongleurs, charmeurs de serpents, danseuses, etc."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "jongleur",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "222e605e-48e2-3422-88c2-133c9a4b1158",
                                        "entry_id": "979a038d-64b1-350d-af8d-88ffb44bd218",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Celui qui jongle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "318d0911-2c4b-3bbc-b8ed-c35d3fdffd19",
                                        "entry_id": "979a038d-64b1-350d-af8d-88ffb44bd218",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Celui qui jongle dans un spectacle de cirque."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "especially"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba6638bf-a9bb-4cbd-9de1-53ad34c321db",
                                                "sense_id": "318d0911-2c4b-3bbc-b8ed-c35d3fdffd19",
                                                "text": "Bastien travaillait un passing de massues avec Rémi et j'en ai compté sept. L'une d'elles montait toujours plus haut que les autres et les bras faisaient des mouvements continus, les massues émettant un bruit clair et creux lorsqu'elles claquaient contre les mains des jongleurs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "495f8e53-d1b7-4e07-9d71-20ec038ab482",
                                                "sense_id": "318d0911-2c4b-3bbc-b8ed-c35d3fdffd19",
                                                "text": "L’écuyère est folle d’amour\nPour un jongleur doux et charmant\nQui ne remarque pas sa cour\nEt jongle avec ses sentiments."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cfda9cb8-9339-3bcb-a3a0-5040332f04c3",
                                        "entry_id": "979a038d-64b1-350d-af8d-88ffb44bd218",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Tout homme qui cherche à en imposer par de fausses apparences."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "familiar",
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fc576a59-8adf-3411-9113-dc21c609fc58",
                                        "entry_id": "979a038d-64b1-350d-af8d-88ffb44bd218",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Espèce de devin guérisseur."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4f4a6988-3c52-4105-ac11-5c30208d307f",
                                                "sense_id": "fc576a59-8adf-3411-9113-dc21c609fc58",
                                                "text": "«cette persuasion est si générale & si incarnée, qu’il n’y a pas une Nation de l'Amérique dans toute son étendue, qui n’ait ses Devins, ou ses Jongleurs, pas une qui n’apprehende les sorts, pas une, ou personne refuse de recourir aux Jongleurs, & ne subisse volontiers toutes les épreuves des Initiations, pour etre fait Jongleur soi-même."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
